README for the VETTAM unit test suite
(source/Simulation/SimulationMain/unitTest/VETTAM)
AUTHOR: Shyam Harimohan Menon (2021)
Reference: VETTAM Method Paper (Menon et al 2022, MNRAS 512, 401)
############################################################################################################

run_tests.py is the test driver. It builds the VETTAM verification problems,
compares each against its analytic solution, and returns a pass/fail status.
Use it for quick verification after changing the module.

Setup targets are unitTest/VETTAM/<Simulation>, e.g.

  ./setup unitTest/VETTAM/Streaming_Pulse -1d -auto -nxb=8 +bouchut

though run_tests.py issues those itself. Parfiles live in parfiles/.

These are the 1-D tests from the method paper. The 3-D ones (RHDThinShell and
the Rosen et al. shadow tests) are not included: they are built on the legacy
RadTransMain/VET unit rather than VETTAM, and are not part of this release.

Running the tests
-----------------

  ./run_tests.py                     quick suite: ~3 min including builds
  ./run_tests.py --full              adds the advection test (hours)
  ./run_tests.py --test diffusion    one test
  ./run_tests.py --compile-only      build only; the cheapest smoke test
  ./run_tests.py --no-compile        reuse existing objdirs
  ./run_tests.py --overwrite         rerun even if outputs exist
  ./run_tests.py --plots             also write diagnostic figures
  ./run_tests.py --list

Stored output is reused between invocations, but only when it is trustworthy:
if flash4 or the parfile is newer than the saved plotfiles, that case is rerun
automatically and says so. Reusing output from an older binary is how the
diffusion test once appeared to have a 1500% error, so this is checked rather
than left to --overwrite. In practice, rebuild the module and rerun with
--no-compile and only the affected cases will actually execute.

Exits 0 if everything is inside tolerance and 1 otherwise, so it can gate a
commit. Every number it computes is written to unitTest_metrics.json, so a
regression can be diffed rather than guessed at. Requires numpy and h5py only
(deliberately not yt, so it stays fast and dependency-light). Object
directories objVETTAM_* are created at the FLASH root; the FLASH tree is found
by walking up from this script, or set --flash-dir / FLASH_DIR.

Tests registered:

  streaming    Free-streaming pulse (Fig. 1 left). Must advect at exactly c
               with radiation energy conserved. Checks propagation speed,
               energy drift and L1 against the rigidly shifted profile.
  diffusion    Diffusing pulse at rho*kappa = 40 and 4e4 cm^-1 (Fig. 1 middle,
               right), compared against the analytic Gaussian spreading
               solution. A third case, "skipgate", reruns the weak setup with
               rt_dt_maxvel lowered so VETTAM's update gate skips ~4 of every 5
               hydro steps, and asserts the pulse width still follows
               sqrt(1/(2 nu^2) + 2 D t). That is a regression guard for BUG-10
               (see the module's BUGS.md): with that bug the width comes out 53%
               short, against ~3% when correct. The plain weak and strong cases
               both pass with the bug present, which is why it exists.
  marshak      Su & Olson (1996) Marshak wave (Fig. 4). Compares E_r and a_R T^4
               against tau_{0.1,1,10,100}.dat at the dumps nearest those
               dimensionless times, tau = epsilon*c*rho*kappa*t. tau=0.1 is
               measured but not asserted on: the earliest dump sits at
               tau ~ 0.117 and there is no closer one, so that comparison
               reflects the time offset rather than solver error. Ported off the
               legacy Cool unit on 2026-10-20; its cool_hydro_update.F90
               override existed only to add a closed-form temperature update for
               c_v = alpha*T^3, now rt_temp_type=5 with rt_cv_alpha, which
               Simulation_initBlock sets to 4*a_r/sim_epsilon.
  radshock     Lowrie & Edwards (2008) M=3 radiation shock (Fig. 5). Checks the
               gas and radiation temperature profiles against the semi-analytic
               solution in Radiation_Shock_LE/M03.0_soln.out; the lab-frame
               moments are transformed to the comoving frame first. Ported off
               the legacy Cool unit on 2026-10-19, which needed two things
               VETTAM now has: per-face Dirichlet radiation temperatures
               (rt_boundary_T_xl/xr/...) and dust_opacity_ir="Constant", a
               total extinction coefficient that skips the dust-to-gas scaling
               and the thermal sputtering cutoff. Simulation_init supplies both
               from the dimensionless inputs, so the 2841-line cool_vet.F90
               override the test used to carry is gone.
  radtempeq_lin
               The same problem and the same parfiles as radtempeq, but built
               with the LinTempUpdate overrides via
               -unit=physics/RadTrans/RadTransMain/VETTAM/LinTempUpdate. Those
               replace the outer Picard/Newton-Raphson temperature iteration
               with a fully coupled linearised solve: the gas temperature
               becomes an extra matrix unknown (NDIM+2 per cell) with the
               a_r T^4 emission linearised about T^n, and rt_dustTemperature
               does nothing but re-run the EOS. rt_hydro_type and rt_temp_type
               are inert in that build.
               Both schemes have to land on the same equilibrium, because that
               is fixed by energy conservation, but they differ during the
               relaxation (about 1 per cent at the first dump for P = 10), so
               this is an independent discretisation measured against the same
               analytic answer rather than a rerun of the same code.
  radtempeq    Radiation-gas equilibration over 20 decades in the radiation to
               gas energy ratio (Fig. 3). Must relax to the temperature implied
               by total energy conservation. Runs on ONE rank: the domain is a
               single 8-cell block, so extra ranks own nothing and the PETSc
               solve stalls.
  advection    Dynamic diffusion, Krumholz et al. 2007 (Fig. 6). Hours; only
               energy conservation is asserted. Use --full.

Not registered: RHDThinShell, Rosen_SinkTest
and Rosen_ShadowBlobs all REQUIRE the legacy RadTransMain/VET or
Cool/CoolMain/RadTransVET unit, not VETTAM. Porting them means rewriting their
simulation-level cool_hydro_update.F90 / cool_vet.F90 overrides. Until then
VETTAM has no automated 3D or sink-particle coverage here; for compile coverage
of those paths use a production setup, e.g.
  ./setup Ionize_HIIRegion -3d -auto -nxb=8 -nyb=8 -nzb=8 +bouchut +bhtree


Parfile repairs (2026-09-30)
----------------------------

The VETTAM parfiles in Menon21Parfiles/ were rewritten because most of the
suite was not exercising VETTAM at all. Four failure modes, all silent:

1. cool_* vs rt_*. VETTAM reads rt_*; the legacy Cool/CoolMain/RadTransVET unit
   reads cool_*. RadPulseStreaming.par, RadTempEq_*.par and Advection_Pulse_*.par
   still used the old names, so VETTAM ran entirely on defaults. useCool does
   not enable it either -- useRadTrans does. Streaming aborted on startup as a
   result (rt_etens defaulted to "vet", which needs the ray tracer); RadTempEq
   and Advection ran with radiation switched off.
2. TreeRay shares the rt_ prefix. rt_computeDt, rt_dtFactor, rt_irradiation,
   rt_nPhi, rt_dirX, rt_ALI, rt_PPM_*, rt_healpix_* belong to TreeRay.
   rt_dtFactor exists in BOTH units, so the TreeRay block was silently setting
   VETTAM's.
3. Duplicate keys: FLASH takes the LAST assignment. RadPulseStrongDiffusion.par
   set dust_iropac_value in a preamble and again in the body, so it had been
   running the weak-diffusion opacity all along, not the strong one.
4. No arithmetic. sim_eddvalue = 1./3. parses as 1.0, not 0.3333.

Also note rt_etens="edd" OVERWRITES XXED with 1/3 every step. A test that sets
its own Eddington factor in the initial conditions (streaming wants f = 1) must
use rt_etens="user", which leaves XXED alone. With "edd" the streaming pulse
travels at c/sqrt(3).

FLASH logs "ignoring unknown parameter" for typos but NOT for a valid parameter
belonging to another unit, which is why all of this passed unnoticed.

The originals are recoverable from git; the pre-rewrite README is kept as
README.orig.bak.


Diagnostic plots
----------------

--plots writes one PDF per test to ./figures (override with --plot-dir). Each
figure overlays the numerical solution on its analytic counterpart and is
annotated with the measured L1 error beside the value published in Menon et al.
2022, so agreement or drift is visible in the figure itself. Current agreement:

  streaming       L1 0.070, 0.159, 0.277   vs published 0.037, 0.160, 0.277
  weak diffusion  L1 0.020, 0.029, 0.032   vs published 0.050, 0.037, 0.033
  strong diff.    L1 0.030, 0.032, 0.033   vs published 0.024, 0.030, 0.032

The plotting lives in vettam_plots.py, ported from the content of
the method paper's plotting onto the vettam_io reader. It needs matplotlib and
nothing else -- no yt, scipy or flashplotlib -- and is imported lazily, so the
default run stays dependency-light. A figure that fails to render prints a
warning and does not fail the suite.



